\DOC SUBSUMED_ID_MAYCHANGE_TAC

\TYPE {SUBSUMED_ID_MAYCHANGE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves goals stating that the identity relation {(=)} is subsumed by a
{MAYCHANGE}-style state-component relation built from {ASSIGNS} components
combined with {,,}.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal whose conclusion is {(=) subsumed t},
where {t} is a single {ASSIGNS} term or a {,,}-chain of such terms, it closes
the goal outright; the assumptions {A} are untouched and play no role in the
outcome.
{
   A ?- (=) subsumed t
   =================== SUBSUMED_ID_MAYCHANGE_TAC
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, only this outcome occurs, on conclusions of exactly
that shape, with the subsuming relation ranging over single components and long
{,,}-chains alike.

\ENDDOC
